WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.960
Jai Shri Mataji! Today I would like to share a couple

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.580
of new improvements, changes on the portal that have appeared recently.

3
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.380
All of this is in the "▶ View translation" mode.

4
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.620
So let's go into it

5
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.200
and see what has appeared here.

6
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:31.340
The first is the ability to change the subtitle size when we watch them

7
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:38.320
full screen. Here is our full-screen mode, we go into it, and

8
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.260
now please notice that there is a little bar here.

9
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:47.670
It disappears together with the cursor after a few seconds of inactivity.

10
00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:53.370
And what does it give us? If you drag it up or down, the subtitles change –

11
00:00:53.530 --> 00:01:00.430
the subtitle size. This way, without leaving

12
00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.630
full-screen mode, you can

13
00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.040
adjust the subtitles.

14
00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:12.370
Even while watching, if you see that the picture has zoomed in close on the face

15
00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:17.130
of Shri Mataji and the subtitles are very large, you can, right in real time, quickly

16
00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.530
drag it a little.

17
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.300
The second thing added here in full-screen mode is that

18
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:33.340
now, when we work in full-screen mode,

19
00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:39.900
pressing the M key, no matter which keyboard layout, Ukrainian

20
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:46.880
or English, and whether it is in English or Ukrainian, creates

21
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:53.840
a marker, to edit the subtitle or to leave a note,

22
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.240
depending on the mode.

23
00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.820
This was there before too.

24
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.900
But now it does not stop playback.

25
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:13.890
In fact, we can watch the talk. If we notice something to correct,

26
00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:18.550
we just press the "M" key, and it does not stop the talk.

27
00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.910
It only leaves a note, so that later, after watching the whole talk,

28
00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.670
we can sit down and work through these notes.

29
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:36.930
You may ask: how do we know that it got there – this note?

30
00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:43.670
At the top left, a barely visible dot will blink when we press it.

31
00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.490
Now I will press the "M" key, see?

32
00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:52.270
The dot blinked a little, depending on whether it is dark mode or light.

33
00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.750
It is a bit more or less visible in light mode, it is greyish.

34
00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.370
This dot blinks.

35
00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.540
Now we will exit full screen,

36
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:11.440
press, and we see that our 6 minutes 16 seconds has been added

37
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.580
here, to the list of subtitles to edit.

38
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:21.010
It works the same for a marker if we are in full-screen mode.

39
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.490
Look at the left corner.

40
00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.580
See, it blinked – I pressed the key.

41
00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.210
In the same way, the marker was added here.

42
00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.960
And one more feature that has appeared in

43
00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.000
this mode

44
00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.580
is the ability to save to your computer.

45
00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.160
What can we save?

46
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.980
"Subtitle file (.srt)". And it will be the subtitle file you have already edited.

47
00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.740
If you have edits, the subtitle file will download with those edits.

48
00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.210
What for – you will think of something.

49
00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:10.500
For example, you want to work in some subtitle editor

50
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.520
of your own.

51
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:19.160
You want the talk with subtitles to work locally, with

52
00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.400
a video file at all.

53
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:26.780
Whatever the goal, it is simply a feature to take the subtitles that

54
00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.340
you see right here on the screen and are working on.

55
00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.400
And

56
00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:40.210
if you still need a video with subtitles, there is now

57
00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:46.300
a feature to create a file with the subtitles already burned in.

58
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:52.520
So even in Telegram, or wherever this file is played, it will have

59
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.900
the subtitles burned in.

60
00:04:54.080 --> 00:05:00.560
And the burned-in subtitles will be the same size you see right here.

61
00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.420
Whatever size you choose here,

62
00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.650
that same size will be put onto the video.

63
00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:16.930
Here we have two creation modes – the full video and a fragment.

64
00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.040
The full video is long here, we will not make it now,

65
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.040
so as not to wait long.

66
00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.020
Let's create a fragment. Why a fragment?

67
00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.940
It is when we want to show an excerpt of a talk with subtitles for a school,

68
00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.880
for example, that can be handy.

69
00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:40.620
And so as not to need extra technical equipment, or to ask someone, or

70
00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.600
anything, we can choose a fragment for ourselves.

71
00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:53.510
When we choose a fragment, the full time is set here by default, but what can we

72
00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:57.850
do? For example, we want to start from this moment.

73
00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:04.150
Let's press "Set the player’s current time", like this, just a moment.

74
00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.310
And, for example,

75
00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.630
we take a short fragment,

76
00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.620
here we set the minute

77
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.820
4 seconds and press "Create the video fragment with subtitles".

78
00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:33.640
The player started, that is unexpected, let's make it not start, I have not seen

79
00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.640
that before.

80
00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.000
Now what happens?

81
00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:43.300
The file is created on the system's side.

82
00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:48.160
That is, it is not created on your computer, but there, in the system.

83
00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.400
And you will simply be able to download it from the system later.

84
00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:56.550
It is kept for seven days, and it is shown to you here in the list

85
00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:02.530
for seven days from the moment it was created.

86
00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:07.000
After that you can start it again.

87
00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:13.090
So this is not an instant process, see, it is starting now.

88
00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.060
When it starts, it will also show a link.

89
00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.460
You will see it now,

90
00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.780
I hope.

91
00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:27.920
And this way you can use the system.

92
00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.780
It has started working, and you can press "View run".

93
00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:37.870
The subtitle burn-in has been working for a minute already.

94
00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:42.770
It downloads the whole video, see, it is just a big video, and first it downloads

95
00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.070
the whole video. This is so that you do not have to do it yourself:

96
00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:53.090
it happens in the background. No need to download a big video,

97
00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.010
or to work in it, no need for a burn-in program.

98
00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.820
When it has downloaded,

99
00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:09.510
the video with subtitles will be created, and there will be the final result.

100
00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:10.970
We will see it now.

101
00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.410
Here we see the download has finished,

102
00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.640
the burn-in is under way.

103
00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.620
This is not something you need to follow in normal use.

104
00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:27.100
For you there are just some steps here

105
00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:36.340
in the interface, and that's it. When it has finished here, you get in the list

106
00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:43.160
a video like this. You can see when it happened – 22.11, 19:49.

107
00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:51.200
The subtitle size was 115%, slightly enlarged. And this is the fragment, from 6:16

108
00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:57.610
to 7:40. And accordingly we can download this video.

109
00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.380
It came out at 4 megabytes.

110
00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.920
That's it, there is the video fragment.

111
00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:27.110
And not about today, nor about the light.

112
00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.450
Do you see?
